            {
                "entry_id": "f151885b-6382-3f09-b094-19a638e93f89",
                "word": "donnant-donnant",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "49f8c3ac-aeab-4c91-b6c9-b756082663d0",
                        "entry_id": "f151885b-6382-3f09-b094-19a638e93f89",
                        "tags": [],
                        "form": "donnant donnant"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "5abe4c9b-8a17-32f9-9134-7ad80b3063d5",
                        "entry_id": "f151885b-6382-3f09-b094-19a638e93f89",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Échange de bons procédés, transaction où une chose n’est donnée qu’à condition d’en recevoir une autre."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c13ee7aa-338b-4542-bfd5-22b1b6c95b51",
                                "sense_id": "5abe4c9b-8a17-32f9-9134-7ad80b3063d5",
                                "text": "Avec en ligne de mire la question de la guerre des prix destructrice de valeur et source de revenus non rémunérateurs pour les agriculteurs. Le président de la République avait alors évoqué une forme de donnant-donnant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "71d94dc0-4e6b-4600-92b8-5d5ac6564f8d",
                                "sense_id": "5abe4c9b-8a17-32f9-9134-7ad80b3063d5",
                                "text": "Il en ressort que l’une des meilleures stratégies, si ce n’est la meilleure stratégie, est celle du donnant-donnant (tit for tat en anglais), consistant à coopérer au départ, puis à reproduire le comportement de l’autre joueur aux tours suivants."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "028553b1-9fe3-4988-bd92-ea9b73bfec82",
                                "sense_id": "5abe4c9b-8a17-32f9-9134-7ad80b3063d5",
                                "text": "Agustín Gonzalez aussi était impliqué, mais jusqu’alors il avait évité la prison en versant une caution exorbitante, et il brûlait ses dernières cartouches en faisant jouer ses relations et le donnant-donnant."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "09758ec9-b6be-4823-88a8-1b829b4e6d0d",
                        "source_entry_id": "f151885b-6382-3f09-b094-19a638e93f89",
                        "source_sense_id": "5abe4c9b-8a17-32f9-9134-7ad80b3063d5",
                        "target_lang_word": "quid pro quo",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "quid pro quo",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c448c349-abc6-372e-b26c-fb761632778f",
                                        "entry_id": "77d04688-5eed-35f4-9606-419e5b589f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which is understood as something else; an equivocation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d40ad21-cf51-4045-a9e0-f981daabc226",
                                                "sense_id": "c448c349-abc6-372e-b26c-fb761632778f",
                                                "text": "The misunderstanding of the word or the quid pro quo is the unintentional pun, and is related to it exactly as folly is to wit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6e99ce4a-4ab2-4b60-9b33-161fe65a9d01",
                                                "sense_id": "c448c349-abc6-372e-b26c-fb761632778f",
                                                "text": "“Is it simply a wild fantasy, or a mistake on the part of the old man — some impossible quid pro quo?”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58895b7c-fa5d-4c1c-a39c-12f68dca8df4",
                                                "sense_id": "c448c349-abc6-372e-b26c-fb761632778f",
                                                "text": "His argument was formulated, not without reason, as a paradox, a quid pro quo of opposing concepts: form is declared to be content, thus its own opposite."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ff045d9e-55a0-3e48-938b-e2aeda33fed1",
                                        "entry_id": "77d04688-5eed-35f4-9606-419e5b589f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Substitution of one drug for another."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ecf0d1b-a2cc-43c1-a0d2-7141097a4f83",
                                                "sense_id": "ff045d9e-55a0-3e48-938b-e2aeda33fed1",
                                                "text": "a knave Apothecary that administers the Physick, and makes the medicine, may doe infinite harme, by his old obsolete doses, adulterine druggs, bad mixtures, quid pro quo, etc."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28d140b6-f810-45bc-b20b-f3dde4ef3b11",
                                                "sense_id": "ff045d9e-55a0-3e48-938b-e2aeda33fed1",
                                                "text": "Nicholas [Praepositus] was also the author of a \"Quid pro Quo\", that is an alphabetically arranged catalogue of equivalent drugs, capable of replacing each other, when for any reason one or the other drug was wanting"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ea51e0db-3e1c-42e0-ba9e-5541c256bc0b",
                                                "sense_id": "ff045d9e-55a0-3e48-938b-e2aeda33fed1",
                                                "text": "Was it not Claudius Galenus (130-200 A. D.), the great Roman physician-pharmacist, who was about the very first to prepare a lengthy list of drugs, quid pro quo, a list which remained in use until about the sixteenth century?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca451031-07d0-34ec-8b01-b516ec14233c",
                                        "entry_id": "77d04688-5eed-35f4-9606-419e5b589f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Something which is offered or asked for in exchange for something else."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1e172d30-7134-484f-a4c4-3dd6da5e6925",
                                                "sense_id": "ca451031-07d0-34ec-8b01-b516ec14233c",
                                                "text": "To him I offered a quid pro quo; and meant to give nothing without getting a full equivalent."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ce48cf51-0aa4-44a9-ae2e-b90737b9a41e",
                                                "sense_id": "ca451031-07d0-34ec-8b01-b516ec14233c",
                                                "text": "Whie Demanding Great sacrifices from the workforce, Germany's rulers had proved unable by autumn 1916 to offer a quid pro quo in the form of a military victory, more democracy, or even a modest redistribution of income."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45b73515-1c04-4a38-b947-d295e302fda1",
                                                "sense_id": "ca451031-07d0-34ec-8b01-b516ec14233c",
                                                "text": "the US recently supported the European candidate for the IMF and may receive a quid pro quo"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "61196598-0929-4e2c-826d-9f8eaafb5575",
                                                "sense_id": "ca451031-07d0-34ec-8b01-b516ec14233c",
                                                "text": "McLaren did not want Mercedes to buy Brawn so when the German company insisted, they demanded a quid pro quo that, as far as McLaren are concerned, contains all the positives of a Mercedes involvement but none of the negatives."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1ae38300-40f4-4175-b2e4-90cbf99cf544",
                                                "sense_id": "ca451031-07d0-34ec-8b01-b516ec14233c",
                                                "text": "People don't like to talk about it, but inherent to every relationship there's a quid pro quo— something that's exchanged in return for something else. The quid pro quo can be obvious, such as I give you a salary and in return I expect you to do a good job, or more subtly, I give you a recommendation and in turn expect you'll help me get my expense check processed faster. It's an unspoken system of bartering that goes on in relationships. Women aren't very good at capitalizing on the quid pro quo. Instead, they give away favors and expect little or nothing in return."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                        "entry_id": "77d04688-5eed-35f4-9606-419e5b589f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A usually non-monetary exchange transaction, or series or process of exchange transactions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04888edd-caee-4c48-9d5c-2255d368b3af",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "More importantly, the Chrysler bailout produced a quid pro quo wherein Congress agreed to pass bank deregulation legislation if banks agreed to convert substantial amounts of Chrysler's debt to equity."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbf8c276-c34c-4bca-9e9e-bb697cb6b956",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "The apparent exception at the Temple of Neith at Sais is likely due to an agreement, a quid pro quo, made with Udjahorresnet, not to a failure to enact the command immediately."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fd16b38-0260-4fb3-b3a8-ebb229e8254e",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "The requisite intent is proved by showing a quid pro quo—an expectation of a favorable official act in return for the bribe."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9dfe37c2-e285-400d-8323-97a4c1bc22ff",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "I call it quid pro quo while other authors have described it as “the art of reciprocity.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1593b55d-6b84-47c7-bf41-ff76c9e4b3a4",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "Neither the envelope nor the entry form indicated whether a donation was enclosed. Because there was no obligation to pay to enter the sweepstakes, payments voluntarily sent were fully deductible. No quid pro quo occurred."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e39ae386-ba81-4602-bd7e-18e7545011b4",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "All are based on the concept of quid pro quo, or “this for that” – the exchange of one thing for another. […] In McDonnell, the government alleged a quid pro quo sale of “official action” – payments (the quid) made to McDonnell, the former governor of Virginia, in return for a promise or undertaking by McDonnell to perform an official action (the quo). The Court’s decision focused on the quo side of the equation – a side that does not often receive much scrutiny – analyzing the contours of whether the actions taken by McDonnell constituted illegal “official actions.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "69a0e3ec-ea79-4a15-aba0-653c9f5cdbe5",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "Council says the mayor and a former councilman may have engaged in a \"quid pro quo.\" / […] / Council says, according to a handwritten note, Fey offered to support a pay raise for Mayor Ellis if Ellis would support a raise or a job appointment for Fey's wife, Gina."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66193e52-a561-43b1-a400-223d0e58db73",
                                                "sense_id": "09970111-9191-3ca1-96bb-43059460477e",
                                                "text": "All I'm asking for is a little quid pro quo. You know—you scratch my back, I'll scratch yours."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39801ec8-1756-34f5-abf8-2f372eb80774",
                                        "entry_id": "77d04688-5eed-35f4-9606-419e5b589f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A usually non-monetary exchange transaction, or series or process of exchange transactions.",
                                            "An equal or fair transaction or series of process of exchange transactions; tit for tat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9bfbc168-bc1e-4fcd-80f5-e5d60d017dc1",
                                                "sense_id": "39801ec8-1756-34f5-abf8-2f372eb80774",
                                                "text": "Mr. P. did not consider that branch, strictly and technically speaking, public revenue; at least it did not arise from taxation, because those persons who had paid this money had received a full equivalent for the same; there was a quid pro quo on both sides; and this was not taxation, it was a sale; the parties therefore from whom this money was derived had not been taxed."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c02c6596-8ddc-49d0-ba9f-6cb202896354",
                                                "sense_id": "39801ec8-1756-34f5-abf8-2f372eb80774",
                                                "text": "What we should do, however, is insist that there be a quid pro quo — an equal exchange."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d7de96a-3105-4e0d-a631-c1bdb7537f74",
                                                "sense_id": "39801ec8-1756-34f5-abf8-2f372eb80774",
                                                "text": "Most of those cases were about witness immunity deals (was there a quid pro quo?) or the meaning of quid pro quo in the classic “equality of exchange” sense."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f2425398-0acb-4c49-8172-a8df38bd5efc",
                                                "sense_id": "39801ec8-1756-34f5-abf8-2f372eb80774",
                                                "text": "US-Myanmar relations in the past few years have been largely based on a quid pro quo or tit for tat strategy. Some analysts also call it action for action or give and take strategy."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "38759c92-876b-3317-b88e-5f08f3686474",
                                        "entry_id": "77d04688-5eed-35f4-9606-419e5b589f71",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Sexual harassment in which a person in a workplace implicitly or explicitly requires sexual favours in exchange for something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cb83d972-7e7a-4d0d-bf5f-da09047d9656",
                                                "sense_id": "38759c92-876b-3317-b88e-5f08f3686474",
                                                "text": "A quid pro quo complaint typically is lodged by an employee who has been denied opportunities because he or she refused a perpetrator's sexual advances or by an employee who has been denied opportunities because another employee obtained those opportunities by submitting to a perpetrator's sexual advances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88ccd15e-d185-4c9b-9d25-3368c0bda945",
                                                "sense_id": "38759c92-876b-3317-b88e-5f08f3686474",
                                                "text": "As for a legal remedy to the problem of harassment, the Court found that a proper, well-advertised grievance procedure could be used in a defense where sexual comments and horseplay created a “hostile environment,” but not in the quid pro quo cases that feminist Catharine MacKinnon had dubbed \"put out or get out.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "66c1e3c8-b313-47e3-be47-4cb68daa6b92",
                                                "sense_id": "38759c92-876b-3317-b88e-5f08f3686474",
                                                "text": "American courts have recognized two forms of sexual harassment. In the first, quid pro quo cases, the violation occurs when an employer or supervisor conditions an employment benefit on the employee's providing sexual favors."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "bd086d60-a9d6-4038-ae73-ac0dae2c0590",
                        "source_entry_id": "f151885b-6382-3f09-b094-19a638e93f89",
                        "source_sense_id": "5abe4c9b-8a17-32f9-9134-7ad80b3063d5",
                        "target_lang_word": "tit for tat",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "tit for tat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                        "entry_id": "f2471d8d-6f0a-3e0b-bb60-5754ba1dc213",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Equivalent retribution; an act of returning exactly what one gets; an eye for an eye."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "idiomatic",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b2fbbb0-ae9b-42c2-ad71-17bd1dc9edcc",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "If you hit me, I’ll hit you back; tit for tat."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de9a0cae-d740-45a7-88ff-7f1760e6a704",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "Tit for tat is the policy of cooperating on the first move and then doing whatever the other player did on the previous move. This policy means that tit for tat will defect once after each defection of the other player."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8450666d-e1b1-43a4-ab3a-f0687725aeb1",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "Could it but for a longer Space / Lengthen the Bliſs it let's us taſte, / Who would not doat on't? But alas! / The Joy's too exquiſite to laſt. / Two white Herculean Pillars prop / The tufted Gin, the tempting Snare; / When they divide, then in we pop, / Before we well know where we are. / Then that for this, and tit for tat; / But when the pleaſing Minute's flown, / As uſeleſs it returns the Bait, / And both look fooliſh when 'tis done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "62677919-de39-41fa-b384-47cf0d561657",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "This is but Tit for Tat, young Gentleman. Your Father wanted to get my Eſtate from me; and I have got the Wife he intended for you. All's fair, Sir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b7376e4-93a4-44ff-9ed9-d108c3321e7c",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "\"You'll never get her over like that. You must coax her.\" / \"Coax the devil. Do you think I'm going to be beat by a horse?\" / \"It would only be tit for tat; you beat her, so she has a right to beat you.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8edc9a59-39ab-496b-9aa3-c8632234f35b",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "YVETTE. I have no idea what to make Monsieur for dinner. / FOLLBRAGUET. (beside himself) Well, that's no skin off my ass, damn it! / YVETTE. (snippily, giving him tit for tat) Well, it's certainly no skin off mine, Monsieur!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7e66df37-29d9-4106-80ee-e1f9445cf851",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "As part of the planning for a new initiative on Cuba, the NSC [National Security Council] also revived the concept of \"calibrated response.\" A new staffer was tasked to develop a list of \"tit-for-tats\" with Cuba—which sanctions might be lifted or softened in response to clear steps toward democracy by the [Fidel] Castro regime."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eba3e720-d12b-406d-85ff-94b4609302d2",
                                                "sense_id": "c9e297c2-7568-381c-a2fb-d0104fccac2b",
                                                "text": "China Warns of ‘Tit for Tat’ on iPhone Sales if Trump Starts Trade War"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "tit for tat",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fc759f19-f569-36f5-b778-21048eecdab7",
                                        "entry_id": "cbbc1dfa-cfa1-346c-8fc0-9aa161fbceaf",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A hat."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Cockney",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52f8d6e1-0e4c-463d-8ea4-4e8f209091ed",
                                                "sense_id": "fc759f19-f569-36f5-b778-21048eecdab7",
                                                "text": "Fred came from Cheapside in London – an official Cockney, born within earshot of the bells of St. Mary-le-Bow – and he taught her Cockney rhyming slang. She loved its lighthearted logic: the last word in a common phrase rhymed with the word it was to replace. So \"tit for tat\" was \"hat\", and \"trouble and strife\" was \"wife\". But the best part was that you usually dropped the rhyming words and used only the first words, so \"your wife's hat\" became \"your trouble's titfer\"."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1655a92-6291-47d1-922b-a7971e751384",
                                                "sense_id": "fc759f19-f569-36f5-b778-21048eecdab7",
                                                "text": "Tit for tat hat / The phrase ‘tit for tat’ […] emerged as a rhyme for ‘hat’ in the late nineteenth century and was subsequently condensed to ‘titfer’ around 1930, in which form it enjoyed unparalleled success at a time when virtually everyone wore a hat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "word_linkages": [
                    {
